# Cursor Rules for Talent Assessment Project

## Project Context
This is a Laravel 5.1 application (legacy version) running on PHP 7.4 in Docker containers.

## Critical Constraints
- Laravel 5.1 does NOT have `php artisan test` command - use `vendor/bin/phpunit` instead
- No `UploadedFile` class available - use alternative testing methods
- Excel processing has been replaced with CSV processing due to library compatibility issues
- Always use Docker commands: `docker-compose exec app <command>`
- Laravel 5.1 tinker does NOT support `--execute` flag - use interactive tinker or create test commands

## Laravel Version Compatibility
- This project uses Laravel 5.1 which has limited tinker functionality
- **NEVER use `php artisan tinker --execute`** - it doesn't work on this Laravel version
- **Use direct database queries instead**: `docker-compose exec mysql mysql -u [user] -p[password] [database] -e "SELECT * FROM table;"`
- **For PHP code execution**: Use `docker-compose exec app php -r "echo 'test';"` for simple PHP commands

## Docker Compose Usage
- **Always use Docker Compose for this project** - never run commands directly on the host
- **For production operations**: Use `docker-compose -f docker-compose.production.yml`
- **For development**: Use `docker-compose` (default)
- **When updating files in containers**: Use `docker-compose cp` to copy updated files into running containers

## Database Operations
- **For database queries**: Use `docker-compose exec mysql mysql -u [user] -p[password] [database] -e "QUERY"`
- **For Laravel commands**: Use `docker-compose exec app php artisan [command]`
- **For production database**: Use production credentials from `.env.production`

## File Management
- **When copying files to production containers**: Always use `docker-compose cp` after making changes
- **Database backups**: Store outside the repository (e.g., `/opt/`) to avoid committing sensitive data
- **Environment files**: Use appropriate `.env` file for the environment (`.env.production`, `.env.staging`, etc.)

## Development Workflow
- **Always check which branch you're on** before making changes
- **Use feature branches** for bug fixes and new features
- **Test in development** before deploying to production
- **Create database backups** before running seeders or migrations in production
- **Always fetch and pull main** before starting new branches to avoid missing changes

## Error Handling
- **For "Whoops" errors**: Check Laravel logs with `docker-compose logs app`
- **For database connection issues**: Verify container status with `docker-compose ps`
- **For permission issues**: Use `sudo` when necessary for file operations

## Production Deployment
- **Always create database backups** before making changes
- **Use `--force` flag** for production seeders: `php artisan db:seed --class=SeederName --force`
- **Copy updated files to containers** before running commands
- **Verify changes** with database queries after deployment

## UI/UX Fixes
- **Login form placeholders**: Use `placeholder` attributes instead of separate `<label>` elements for username/password fields
- **Form interactions**: Always test that placeholder text clears when users start typing
- **Reference release versions**: Compare with working release tags (e.g., `v1.5.26-release`) before making UI changes
- **Document UI fixes**: Create documentation in `/docs/` for any UI/UX fixes to prevent regression
- **Asset paths**: Images are now in `public/assets/images/` not `public/images/` - use `{{ asset('assets/images/filename') }}`

## Environment-Specific Docker Compose Rules

### Development Environment
- **Compose file**: `docker-compose.yml`
- **Container prefix**: `talent-assessment-*`
- **Access**: `http://localhost:8001`
- **Commands**: Always use `docker-compose exec app <command>`

### Staging Environment
- **Compose file**: `docker-compose.staging.yml`
- **Container prefix**: `talent-assessment-app-staging`, `talent-assessment-mysql-staging`, `talent-assessment-redis-staging`
- **Access**: `https://talent-staging.cyberworldbuilders.dev`
- **Commands**: Use `docker-compose -f docker-compose.staging.yml exec app-staging <command>`
- **Deployment**: Automated via GitHub Actions

### Production Environment
- **Compose file**: `docker-compose.production.yml`
- **Container prefix**: `talent-assessment-app-production`, `talent-assessment-mysql-production`, `talent-assessment-redis-production`
- **Access**: `https://talent.cyberworldbuilders.dev`
- **Commands**: Use `docker-compose -f docker-compose.production.yml exec app-production <command>`
- **Deployment**: Manual via SSH

## Testing Guidelines
- Use `docker-compose exec app vendor/bin/phpunit` for tests
- Use `DatabaseTransactions` trait for database tests
- Test CSV parsing logic directly rather than file uploads
- Create temporary files for file-based tests

## File Upload System
- User bulk uploads now use CSV format (converted from Excel)
- Endpoint: POST /dashboard/users/upload
- Controller: UsersController@upload_from_file
- Validation: accepts .csv and .txt files

## Code Style
- Follow Laravel 5.1 conventions
- Use existing patterns in codebase
- Maintain backward compatibility
- Document breaking changes

## Common Commands

### Development Environment
```bash
# Run tests
docker-compose exec app vendor/bin/phpunit

# Run specific test
docker-compose exec app vendor/bin/phpunit tests/UserCsvUploadTest.php

# Access container
docker-compose exec app bash

# Artisan commands
docker-compose exec app php artisan <command>

# View logs
docker-compose logs app
```

### Staging Environment
```bash
# Run tests
docker-compose -f docker-compose.staging.yml exec app-staging vendor/bin/phpunit

# Access container
docker-compose -f docker-compose.staging.yml exec app-staging bash

# Artisan commands
docker-compose -f docker-compose.staging.yml exec app-staging php artisan <command>

# View logs
docker-compose -f docker-compose.staging.yml logs app-staging
```

### Production Environment
```bash
# Access container (be very careful!)
docker-compose -f docker-compose.production.yml exec app-production bash

# Artisan commands (be very careful!)
docker-compose -f docker-compose.production.yml exec app-production php artisan <command>

# View logs
docker-compose -f docker-compose.production.yml logs app-production

# Check container status
docker-compose -f docker-compose.production.yml ps
```

